    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`nextCustomerCode`** now takes both `city` and `lastName`. It builds `CITY3` (upper-cased first three letters of the city), `LAST3` (upper-cased first three of the last name), and `NNNN` \u2014 a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the owners already in that city.\n- Added **`countOwnersInCity`**, which counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (mirroring the existing `countNamesakes` helper).\n- The **membership number** is derived from the customer code (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`) \u2014 no separate change needed beyond the call already passing `owner.getCustomerCode()`.\n- Updated the surrounding comments and Javadoc examples to reflect the new format.\n\n`./mvnw test` passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (`AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, which asserts the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`), **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
